Accent marks for 0x__41 to 0x__5A and 0x__61 to 0x__7A will have the high
nybble changed from 0x2 to one of the below (for Latin-based alphabets):
  0x2___ = no accent mark
  0x3___ = acute
  0x4___ = grave
  0x5___ = umlaut
  0x6___ = circumflex
  0x8___ = tilde
  0x9___ = dot
  0xA___ = ring
  0xB___ = caron

(Greek and Cyrillic alphabets might use a different set of accent marks.
This does not include all accent marks because they do not all fit into
this plane (although they might do later if some parts of the secondly
high nybble are also used for accent marks), but other planes are available
for more elaborate sets of accented alphabets. This plane mostly has the
ones commonly used on older computers, but is not only limited to that.)

