0x8A80 to 0x8ABF and 0x8B80 to 0x8BBF are also the seven segment displays
but with the lower right dot added.

Horizontal/vertical line drawing: Start with 0x9080, but add the numbers:
  0x0001 = line to right
  0x0002 = line to left
  0x0004 = line to top
  0x0008 = line to bottom
  0x0010 = double horizontal lines
  0x0020 = double vertical lines
If there are no lines, then a middle dot should be shown. (The range of
these line drawings are therefore 0x9080 to 0x90BF.) (Also note that the
single vertical line should line up with the halfs of the integral sign.)

0x90C4 = bottom half of integral sign
0x90C8 = top half of integral sign

0x90F1 to 0x90F7 = NEC APC dashed line drawing 0xF1 to 0xF7:
  dashed horizontal
  dashed vertical
  solid horizontal and dashed up
  solid horizontal and dashed down
  solid vertical and dashed left
  solid vertical and dashed right
  dashed horizontal and dashed vertical

